# Use Cases

Use cases (`*_use_case.dart`) encapsulate a single business operation. They are `@injectable` classes with a `call()` method, injected into Store and State classes via constructor dependency injection.

## Anatomy

```dart
@injectable
class CreateTagUseCase {
  final DioService _dioService;
  final IssueTrackingService _issueTrackingService;

  CreateTagUseCase(this._dioService, this._issueTrackingService);

  Future<String?> call(String name, String color) async {
    // single operation
  }
}
```

Key points:
- Annotate with `@injectable` (never `@singleton` unless the use case itself holds state — rare)
- Name follows `*UseCase` pattern, file follows `*_use_case.dart`
- Method is named `call()` — Dart's magic method making the object directly callable: `await useCase(name, color)`
- Constructor injection only — no `getIt<>()` calls inside

## 4 Types

### 1. API Use Case
Wraps one API call, handles `DioException`, maps to domain objects or error types.

```dart
@injectable
class CreateTagUseCase {
  final DioService _dioService;
  final IssueTrackingService _issueTrackingService;

  CreateTagUseCase(this._dioService, this._issueTrackingService);

  Future<String?> call(String name, String color) async {
    try {
      final response = await _dioService.tagsProvider.createTag(
        tagCreateDto: TagCreateUpdateRequestDto(name: name, color: color),
      );
      return response.data.id;
    } on DioException catch (e) {
      _issueTrackingService.trackIssue(e);
      final dto = _issueTrackingService.getDioExceptionDto(e);
      if (dto?.errorCode == ServerErrorCode.TAG_ALREADY_EXISTS) {
        throw TagAlreadyCreatedException(dto?.message.tr());
      }
    }
    return null;
  }
}
```

### 2. Navigation Use Case
Wraps `AppNavigator` calls to open modals, dialogs, or push routes.

```dart
@injectable
class ShowStorageIsFullModalUseCase {
  final AppNavigator _appNavigator;

  ShowStorageIsFullModalUseCase(this._appNavigator);

  void call() {
    _appNavigator.showModal(builder: (_) => const StorageIsFullModal());
  }
}
```

### 3. Service Coordination Use Case
Orchestrates 2+ services or platform calls in a single logical operation.

```dart
@injectable
class StartRecordingUseCase {
  final AudioService _audioService;
  final PermissionService _permissionService;
  final IssueTrackingService _issueTrackingService;

  StartRecordingUseCase(
    this._audioService,
    this._permissionService,
    this._issueTrackingService,
  );

  Future<bool> call() async {
    final granted = await _permissionService.requestMicrophone();
    if (!granted) return false;
    try {
      await _audioService.startRecording();
      return true;
    } catch (e) {
      _issueTrackingService.trackIssue(e);
      return false;
    }
  }
}
```

### 4. State Delegation Use Case
Encapsulates a conditional flow or guard logic called from many callers.

```dart
@injectable
class HandleDeepLinkUseCase {
  final AppNavigator _appNavigator;
  final AuthStore _authStore;

  HandleDeepLinkUseCase(this._appNavigator, this._authStore);

  void call(Uri link) {
    if (!_authStore.isLoggedIn) {
      _appNavigator.push(const LoginRoute());
      return;
    }
    // route to correct screen
  }
}
```

## Location Rules

| Scope | Path |
|---|---|
| Used only within one feature | `lib/features/{feature}/use_cases/` |
| Used within a feature's core (e.g. by a feature store + its state) | `lib/features/{feature}/core/use_cases/` |
| Consumed by a specific shared store and its callers | `lib/shared/stores/{store}/use_cases/` |
| Shared across many unrelated features | `lib/core/use_cases/` |

## Calling Use Cases

Because `call()` is Dart's magic method, use cases are invoked directly without `.call()`:

```dart
// ✅ Direct call syntax
final id = await _createTagUseCase(name, color);
_showStorageFullUseCase();

// ❌ Avoid — verbose and unnecessary
await _createTagUseCase.call(name, color);
```

## Injection into Stores and States

### In a Store

```dart
abstract class _TagsStoreBase with Store {
  final CreateTagUseCase _createTagUseCase;

  _TagsStoreBase(this._createTagUseCase);

  @action
  Future<void> createTag(String name, String color) async {
    final id = await _createTagUseCase(name, color);
    if (id != null) {
      // update observable state
    }
  }
}
```

### In a State class

```dart
abstract class _SettingsPageStateBase with Store {
  final ShowStorageIsFullModalUseCase _showStorageFullUseCase;

  _SettingsPageStateBase(this._showStorageFullUseCase);

  @action
  void onStorageWarningTap() {
    _showStorageFullUseCase();
  }
}
```

## Decision Tree: Use Case vs Inline

```
Is the logic reused in 2+ Stores or States?
  YES → Extract use case

Does the operation coordinate 2+ services or async steps?
  YES → Extract use case

Is the logic complex enough to warrant its own test?
  YES → Extract use case

Is it a trivial one-liner delegation?
  YES → Keep inline
```

## Common Mistakes

- **`@singleton` on a use case**: Only use if the use case itself manages state (very rare). Default is `@injectable`.
- **Over-extracting trivial logic**: A single `_dioService.someProvider.fetch()` call with no error handling is fine inline in the store.
- **Calling `getIt<>()` inside a use case**: Never. Always inject via constructor.
- **Forgetting code generation**: After adding a new `@injectable` use case, run `melos run build_all` to regenerate DI code.
- **Using `execute()` instead of `call()`**: All use cases in this project use `call()` so they can be invoked directly.
